Z||000007||Voytek||03-15-2001||05:28 PM||||I wouldn't be so certain that it IS the tach filter.  When I bought my '87 GT 4 years ago, it was real beat up.  The tach was jumping up and down all the time.  The problem went away after I changed the spark plugs - they were all fouled up and burnt.  Because it's a V6, it generally runs pretty smooth, even if some cylinders occasionally miss.  This is a fairly easy and inexpensive job - I would start there (unless you know that the plugs are new??)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||03-15-2001||05:43 PM||||Rodney Dickman sells the tach filters.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
